{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364158-player-wants-to-make-a-character-that-can-make-paintings-come-to-life","id":1364158,"title":"Player wants to make a character that can make paintings come to life!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-30T07:55:08-08:00","id":1364158,"title":"Player wants to make a character that can make paintings come to life!","content":"Hello all, <br /> <br /> Brand new exalted St here. I have a player that wants to make a character like Rill (from black clover) or Relm from ff4, what would allow him to do this? <br /> <br /> Thank you in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5059-johnsonhavoc","name":"johnsonhavoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T08:14:34-08:00","id":1364160,"title":"","content":"Sounds like sorcery, with some craft based shaping rituals, and some reskinning of spells to be paintings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T08:22:44-08:00","id":1364161,"title":"","content":"There's a few ways to approach this, all of which will require some homebrewing. <br /> <br /> The first is native charms of some type of Exalt. I could see this being an effect that fit in with either Solar or Dragon-Blooded Craft. For Solars, the logic would be &quot;I can paint something so well it <i>literally</i> comes to life&quot;, while for Dragon-Blooded it would be &quot;I can imbue my paintings with elemental power that animate them&quot;. I could see Lunars getting a similar effect as well, though I'd probably put that in Charisma or Intelligence for them, and the effect would be a bit broader, along the lines of &quot;things I describe or depict are so realistic that they become animated&quot;.<br /> <br /> Second, you could make an artifact - a magic paintbrush, for instance. I'd put an artifact that can animate the images of what it paints at Artifact 3, while one that can actually summon physical things would be Artifact 4.<br /> <br /> Finally, you could go for the Exigent option. This will require the most homebrewing, as it basically means you're creating a whole new type of Exalted, with their own custom charmset. But if the player wants this to be their whole thing, then being the Exigent of the God of Paintings or something like that is probably the best way to get a powerset that makes this central.<br /> <br /> So, which option do you think works best for your player?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T08:38:44-08:00","id":1364163,"title":"","content":"My first thought reading this was 4 or 5 dot artifact. They're the ones you can build a character around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T08:50:36-08:00","id":1364164,"title":"","content":"How much does the player want to focus on this? Do they want painting to be their character's main 'thing', their power that affects their entire build? Or are they okay with it being a more limited, focused ability, allowing them to do other stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T08:51:29-08:00","id":1364165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364158-player-wants-to-make-a-character-that-can-make-paintings-come-to-life?p=1364160#post1364160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like sorcery, with some craft based shaping rituals, and some reskinning of spells to be paintings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorcery is an excellent point as well, yeah. You could make a custom initiation for them, and justify a <i>lot</i> of spells as being paintings. If they take any summoning spells (Demon of the 1st/2nd/3rd Circle or Summon Elemental), I'd allow a custom merit that lets them paint their summoned creature, customizing its appearance and just using the stats from various existing creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T08:55:07-08:00","id":1364166,"title":"","content":"See, I'm tempted to reccomended Survival and Craft. Craftsman Needs No Tools already lets you make whatever without the gear. A custom expansion charm to let you craft anything with 1 ability isn't that unreasonable. Then you use survival to fight with the animals you painted from your ninja beast scroll!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T09:01:42-08:00","id":1364168,"title":"","content":"All of these are great! Thank you. I do think the sorcery idea would be cool and easiest, what rating would you make the merit? <br /> <br /> Though I am still open to ideas. I just asked him what kind of concept he was looking into and told me this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5059-johnsonhavoc","name":"johnsonhavoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T09:13:35-08:00","id":1364172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johnsonhavoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364158-player-wants-to-make-a-character-that-can-make-paintings-come-to-life?p=1364168#post1364168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what rating would you make the merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd put it at 1 dot if it just allowed some degree of customizing the summoned creature (a blood ape with green fur instead of red-orange), 3 dots if it allowed fairly radical departures from the default appearance (the blood ape is now a giant stag beetle with huge pincers), or 5 dots if custom appearances allowed some limited custom traits as well (the &quot;blood ape&quot; is a giant stag beetle, and it has a goring horn attack in addition to the blood ape's normal innate weaponry). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T09:13:40-08:00","id":1364173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364158-player-wants-to-make-a-character-that-can-make-paintings-come-to-life?p=1364160#post1364160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like sorcery, with some craft based shaping rituals, and some reskinning of spells to be paintings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably the most by-the-book way to do it.<ul><li><b>Sculpted Seafoam Eidolon</b> (from the Dragonblooded book) is almost exactly what you want-- it lets you create a simulacrum of anything from objects to people, with lifelike traits and basic intelligences.</li> <li><b>Demon of the First Circle</b> and <b>Summon Elemental</b> would also be relevant. Infallible Messenger too, maybe.</li> <li><b>Floral Ferry</b> (the Dragonblooded book again) creates a little ship from essentially nothing; seems fitting to me.</li> </ul>But more fitting, perhaps, would be some of the Charms from Sanctafrax's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\">Craft overhaul</a>. Most of them are still compatible with the default system, and there's lots of good stuff that seems utterly perfect for this character. The whole rewrite is built around the idea of using Craft mid-adventure, so there's some <i>big </i>stuff about creating things really really quickly.<ul><li><b>Words as a Workshop Method</b> literally lets you build stuff out of nothingness, replacing materials with raw Essence. A follow-up Charm (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Art Of Permanence</b>) lets you spend willpower to make them real. That's... what you want. That's exactly what you want.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Living Statue Genesis</b> and its follow-ups, <b>Life From The Workshop</b> and <b>Stone Legion Construction</b>, are <i>technically </i>about animating statues and clockwork soldiers and stuff, but they'd work just as well with life-sized artwork. Boom, bang, pow. Concept filled. But there's more!</span></span></li> <li><b>Craft of War</b> lets you use Craft for in-combat gambits. Say, painting a cage around a dude and trapping him.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Instantaneous Architecture Technique</b> lets you use the former as a simple action to create walls, houses, and bridges even mid-battle.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Painted Truth Prana</b> is literally written for super-painters; it lets you encode social influence into artwork.</span></span></li> <li><b>Glorious Solar Arsenal</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> and </span></span><b>Glorious Solar Armory</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> let you pull artifact weapons and armor out of nowhere. Or, say, a painting.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Heck, you could go farther and flavor more normal, long-term &quot;sit in a workshop and build&quot; Craft as painting too. Just something incredibly large and intricate and perfect, such that it takes weeks to finish even for a Solar.<br /> <br /> EDIT:... now <i>I </i>want to play this character.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 01-30-2020, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T09:38:47-08:00","id":1364182,"title":"","content":"Interesting! Thank you all for the help! If you can think of anything else I will definitely listen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5059-johnsonhavoc","name":"johnsonhavoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T12:47:52-08:00","id":1364208,"title":"","content":"It could also be some kind of spirit Charms learned by an Eclipse Caste Solar, although I think sorcery probably works out better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T12:56:01-08:00","id":1364209,"title":"","content":"Do you have Arms of the Chosen? Might be worth a look at the Distaff, which lets you create people from cloth. I could see similar rules working for making people from paintings come alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T04:38:11-08:00","id":1364317,"title":"","content":"Weren't there charms like this back in 1E? It's been so long I may be misremembering","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T09:07:26-08:00","id":1364359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364158-player-wants-to-make-a-character-that-can-make-paintings-come-to-life?p=1364317#post1364317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't there charms like this back in 1E? It's been so long I may be misremembering</div> </div> </div> </div>There was that group of paintings in the Invisible Fortress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T17:59:33-08:00","id":1364442,"title":"","content":"One of the books -- probably Invisible Fortress, from what TheCountAlucard just said, but I'd have to go check -- had a Solar Craft Charm called World Within a Picture Style that let the user create images people could enter. You could paint a room full of comfortable chairs, then everyone steps into the painting and sits down.<br /> <br /> (IIRC, though, if the picture was destroyed then anyone inside it just fucking died. I thought that was a little ridiculous -- it makes a certain degree of sense, but someone shouldn't be able to kill an Exalt with no resistance by sneaking up and burning a painting.)<br /> <br /> Paintings that people can <i>enter</i> are like the opposite of what the OP asked for, but it was certainly cool (and the same character might learn to do both).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T19:34:46-08:00","id":1364453,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t forget to fill them with the power stars that intruders have to collect to reach your throne room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T04:51:34-08:00","id":1364518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364158-player-wants-to-make-a-character-that-can-make-paintings-come-to-life?p=1364453#post1364453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t forget to fill them with the power stars that intruders have to collect to reach your throne room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intricate mechanical puzzles and further paintings linking you to other, deeper worlds are also acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T06:20:34-08:00","id":1364526,"title":"","content":"Ooo that is pretty cool. Does it translate well from 1e to 3e? <br /> <br /> Thanks again everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5059-johnsonhavoc","name":"johnsonhavoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T13:21:10-08:00","id":1364595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johnsonhavoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364158-player-wants-to-make-a-character-that-can-make-paintings-come-to-life?p=1364526#post1364526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooo that is pretty cool. Does it translate well from 1e to 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing about the function of the Charm is edition-specific.<br /> <br /> So here we go:<br /> <br /> <b>World Within a Picture Style</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 2 gxp; <b>Mins:</b> Craft 5, Occult 3, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Flawless Handiwork Method<br /> <br /> A Solar who has truly mastered some form of representational art -- most commonly painting, but tapestry-weaving, carving, and metal-casting are all possible -- can create an image so lifelike that it may as well be real. The physical matrix of the picture need not be &quot;life size&quot; -- a metal brooch engraved with an incredibly realistic miniature scene would still work.<br /> <br /> Normally, the World Within a Picture cannot exceed one acre in size, although it may appear much larger. (A person who tries to step out of the simulated area either steps out into the real world, or goes in a circle.) The image may contain plants, animals, or even people, but the people are not real -- they react only in simple, stereotyped ways, like automata. Adding realistic sapient beings to the World Within a Picture would require a sorcerous working; trapping an <i>actual</i> sapient being within the still life as a permanent resident might be possible with a spell of the Celestial Circle. All manner of sorcerous workings are possible, if the sorcerer wishes to add strange effects to the environment inside, such as an image which allows visitors to fly or transforms them into different forms.<br /> <br /> Entering a World Within a Picture costs 1 mote; leaving is free. One person may spend additional motes on the behalf of others to allow them entrance. Damaging the picture causes visible cosmetic damage to the world within; if the picture is actually destroyed, any real people inside are ejected into the real world, each suffering one unsoakable level of lethal damage from having the world destroyed around them (a small price to pay, all things considered).<br /> <br /> Creating a World Within a Picture is a major project, and takes as long as the Storyteller judges it would normally take to make a painting or tapestry or whatever. Once created, it lasts until destroyed.<br /> <br /> An Essence 4+ repurchase allows the Solar to spend 10m. 2wxp in place of the usual cost, in exchange for increasing the size limit from one acre to (Essence) square miles.<br /> <br /> A few notes:<br /> - In the original version, if the picture gets damaged anyone inside is trapped until it's repaired, and if the picture is destroyed they're all just dead, consigned to Oblivion. I really didn't like that so I changed it, but figure out what works for you and your group. (Personally, I think that if you want to create a painting-world that acts as a trap and makes it easy for you to imprison or kill anyone who enters, you should need a sorcerous working, or possibly one or more additional Charms.)<br /> - The original version cost 20 motes. I figured that a cost in craft XP made sense in 3e. I didn't want to make it require white XP (requiring characters to make actual artifacts first seems unfair -- if major projects are enough to prepare you to make a daiklave, they're enough to prepare you to make a World Within a Picture), and then I hit on the idea of using white XP to expand on the one-acre limit.<br /> - Flawless Handiwork Method is the same prerequisite it had in 1e. I suspect if it showed up in a 3e product it would have a much longer prerequisite chain, but I couldn't decide on anything appropriate so whatever. I did consider adding Terrestrial Circle Sorcery to the prerequisites, since it already required Occult 3, but eh. A Solar doesn't need to be a sorcerer to master painting to a supernatural degree.<br /> - The original version had a listed duration of &quot;one day or more.&quot; I assume that's a mistake, because it would require committed Essence then.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T14:34:18-08:00","id":1364611,"title":"","content":"Between this and my project converting Spirit Rings from Bo3C, I need to start a thread about bringing very early 1ed stuff to 3ed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T15:08:53-08:00","id":1364616,"title":"","content":"Dreaming Pearl Courtesan style could be very, very easily modified to be calligraphy and paint inspired. The capstone charm would instead be painting your true soul and willing it to life in place of your physical body. <br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of flavor changing existing mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-o