ple, stereotyped ways, like automata. Adding realistic sapient beings to the World Within a Picture would require a sorcerous working; trapping an <i>actual</i> sapient being within the still life as a permanent resident might be possible with a spell of the Celestial Circle. All manner of sorcerous workings are possible, if the sorcerer wishes to add strange effects to the environment inside, such as an image which allows visitors to fly or transforms them into different forms.<br /> <br /> Entering a World Within a Picture costs 1 mote; leaving is free. One person may spend additional motes on the behalf of others to allow them entrance. Damaging the picture causes visible cosmetic damage to the world within; if the picture is actually destroyed, any real people inside are ejected into the real world, each suffering one unsoakable level of lethal damage from having the world destroyed around them (a small price to pay, all things considered).<br /> <br /> Creating a World Within a Picture is a major project, and takes as long as the Storyteller judges it would normally take to make a painting or tapestry or whatever. Once created, it lasts until destroyed.<br /> <br /> An Essence 4+ repurchase allows the Solar to spend 10m. 2wxp in place of the usual cost, in exchange for increasing the size limit from one acre to (Essence) square miles.<br /> <br /> A few notes:<br /> - In the original version, if the picture gets damaged anyone inside is trapped until it's repaired, and if the picture is destroyed they're all just dead, consigned to Oblivion. I really didn't like that so I changed it, but figure out what works for you and your group. (Personally, I think that if you want to create a painting-world that acts as a trap and makes it easy for you to imprison or kill anyone who enters, you should need a sorcerous working, or possibly one or more additional Charms.)<br /> - The original version cost 20 motes. I figured that a cost in craft XP made sense in 3e. I didn't want to make it require white XP (requiring characters to make actual artifacts first seems unfair -- if major projects are enough to prepare you to make a daiklave, they're enough to prepare you to make a World Within a Picture), and then I hit on the idea of using white XP to expand on the one-acre limit.<br /> - Flawless Handiwork Method is the same prerequisite it had in 1e. I suspect if it showed up in a 3e product it would have a much longer prerequisite chain, but I couldn't decide on anything appropriate so whatever. I did consider adding Terrestrial Circle Sorcery to the prerequisites, since it already required Occult 3, but eh. A Solar doesn't need to be a sorcerer to master painting to a supernatural degree.<br /> - The original version had a listed duration of &amp;quot;one day or more.&amp;quot; I assume that's a mistake, because it would require committed Essence then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5059-johnsonhavoc","name":"johnsonhavoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T18:31:47-08:00","id":1366449,"title":"","content":"Alight my friends! <br /> <br /> Finally got to talk with my player and he has decided that sorcercy would be best. <br /> <br /> What I need help on if anyone is willing to help is working on a custom shaping for it. <br /> <br /> Anyone willing to help a newbie st out and draft one up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5059-johnsonhavoc","name":"johnsonhavoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T19:29:24-08:00","id":1366453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johnsonhavoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364158-player-wants-to-make-a-character-that-can-make-paintings-come-to-life?p=1366449#post1366449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alight my friends!<br /> <br /> Finally got to talk with my player and he has decided that sorcercy would be best.<br /> <br /> What I need help on if anyone is willing to help is working on a custom shaping for it.<br /> <br /> Anyone willing to help a newbie st out and draft one up?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If we're thinking of spells flavored as coming from paintings then the obvious thing for them to do to gain sorcerous motes is, well, painting. That sounds like a slow process done in advance, which reminds me of this shaping ritual from the core book (and WFHW):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">The sorcerer has been tutored in the arcane arts at the </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Heptagram or a similar sorcerous academy. Once per story, </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">she may perform sorcerous research and then roll (Intelligence + Lore), gaining sorcerous motes equal to the successes that last for that story\u2019s duration. Access to a library or a mentor adds one to two bonus dice to this roll. </span> </div> </div> </div>I would modify it as follows:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">The sorcerer's spells are paintings that come to life</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">. Once per story, </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">she may create a new painting and then roll (Intelligence + Craft (Painting)), gaining sorcerous motes equal to the successes that last for that story\u2019s duration. Access to a workshop with quality tools, or other support, adds one to two bonus dice to this roll. </span> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> Or you could go with this, modified from one of the What Fire Has Wrought ones:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">The sorcerer's spells are paintings that come to life. Once per scene, when she stunts the first shape sorcery roll of a spell by describing the painting that is coming to life, she gains (stunt rating + 2) sorcerous motes toward completing the spell. Enhancing her control spell doesn't count towards this once-a-scene limit. </span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T19:46:31-08:00","id":1366454,"title":"","content":"Oh those are awesome ideas! I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5059-johnsonhavoc","name":"johnsonhavoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T13:53:46-08:00","id":1366625,"title":"","content":"With the help of everyone, I made this! What do you all think?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Creation Painting Initiation </b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><i>\u201cEvery artist dips his brush in his own soul, and paints his own nature into his pictures.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The art of the person is the true window into the universe. The sorcerer has tapped into the raw pallet of the world through their painting. The Wyld nature and chaos that lives just beyond creation revealing the magic within and guiding them to inspiring creation with their imagination.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shaping Rituals</span></span></b><ul><li>The sorcerer inspires creation by tapping into the Wyld and giving it form on canvas. Once per story, she may create a new painting and then roll (Intelligence + Craft (Painting)), gaining sorcerous motes equal to the successes that last for that story\u2019s duration. Access to a workshop with quality tools, or other support, adds one to two bonus dice to this roll.</li> </ul><ul><li>The sorcerer's spells are paintings that come to life. Once per scene, when she stunts the first shape sorcery roll of a spell by describing the painting that they created that is coming to life, she gains (stunt rating + 2) sorcerous motes toward completing the spell. Enhancing her control spell doesn't count towards this once-a-scene limit.</li> </ul><ul><li>The sorcerer may feed on inspired energies of people, shaping the passions of others through spellcraft. Once per scene, when another character forms, strengthens, or weakens an Intimacy with their art, the sorcerer may feed from it, gaining sorcerous motes equal to the intensity of the Intimacy (its new rating if it was strengthened, or the old one if weakened). These motes last for the duration of the story and can be spent towards any spell she casts.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other Benefits:</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Paint to Canvas Method (Merit \u2022): </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sorcerors of the Creation Painting Initiation frequently make use of their trade tools such as painting their desired effect onto a canvas, a wall, or even the ground. A sorcerer who makes use of their trade tools while taking Shape Sorcery actions adds +1 die to their pool.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Painted Lotus (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The sorcerer's understanding of the Wyld nature of creation has gifted them the ability to alter the form a spell takes when released in creation. Their imagination alters the spell\u2019s look, color, and size. The sorcerers imagine must still play within the rules of creation cannot work against the theme of a spell. A summoned demon cannot be made to look less of a demon, a water elemental must still be made of water, etc.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Master of Creativity (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>: </b>The sorcerer is immune to the twisting power of the Wyld, and need never fear mutation, delusion, or addiction from time spent in the chaos that inspires them. However, her Wyld affinity makes her vulnerable to iron, causing her to take aggravated damage from weapons made of it as though she were one of the Raksha.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5059-johnsonhavoc","name":"johnsonhavoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T15:35:50-08:00","id":1366644,"title":"","content":"I updated it thanks to some feedback!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19zoZNECHqaz31AIaRLWr_9aoRRC47DaK0xbd6mt7J2M/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19zoZNECHqaz31AIaRLWr_9aoRRC47DaK0xbd6mt7J2M/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19zoZNECHqaz31AIaRLWr_9aoRRC47DaK0xbd6mt7J2M/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/19zoZNECHqaz31AIaRLWr_9aoRRC47DaK0xbd6mt7J2M/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5059-johnsonhavoc","name":"johnsonhavoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T16:02:29-08:00","id":1366651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johnsonhavoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364158-player-wants-to-make-a-character-that-can-make-paintings-come-to-life?p=1366625#post1366625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the help of everyone, I made this! What do you all think?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Creation Painting Initiation </b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><i>\u201cEvery artist dips his brush in his own soul, and paints his own nature into his pictures.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The art of the person is the true window into the universe. The sorcerer has tapped into the raw pallet of the world through their painting. The Wyld nature and chaos that lives just beyond creation revealing the magic within and guiding them to inspiring creation with their imagination.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shaping Rituals</span></span></b><ul><li>The sorcerer inspires creation by tapping into the Wyld and giving it form on canvas. Once per story, she may create a new painting and then roll (Intelligence + Craft (Painting)), gaining sorcerous motes equal to the successes that last for that story\u2019s duration. Access to a workshop with quality tools, or other support, adds one to two bonus dice to this roll.</li> </ul><ul><li>The sorcerer's spells are paintings that come to life. Once per scene, when she stunts the first shape sorcery roll of a spell by describing the painting that they created that is coming to life, she gains (stunt rating + 2) sorcerous motes toward completing the spell. Enhancing her control spell doesn't count towards this once-a-scene limit.</li> </ul><ul><li>The sorcerer may feed on inspired energies of people, shaping the passions of others through spellcraft. Once per scene, when another character forms, strengthens, or weakens an Intimacy with their art, the sorcerer may feed from it, gaining sorcerous motes equal to the intensity of the Intimacy (its new rating if it was strengthened, or the old one if weakened). These motes last for the duration of the story and can be spent towards any spell she casts.</li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other Benefits:</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Paint to Canvas Method (Merit \u2022): </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sorcerors of the Creation Painting Initiation frequently make use of their trade tools such as painting their desired effect onto a canvas, a wall, or even the ground. A sorcerer who makes use of their trade tools while taking Shape Sorcery actions adds +1 die to their pool.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Painted Lotus (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The sorcerer's understanding of the Wyld nature of creation has gifted them the ability to alter the form a spell takes when released in creation. Their imagination alters the spell\u2019s look, color, and size. The sorcerers imagine must still play within the rules of creation cannot work against the theme of a spell. A summoned demon cannot be made to look less of a demon, a water elemental must still be made of water, etc.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Master of Creativity (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>: </b>The sorcerer is immune to the twisting power of the Wyld, and need never fear mutation, delusion, or addiction from time spent in the chaos that inspires them. However, her Wyld affinity makes her vulnerable to iron, causing her to take aggravated damage from weapons made of it as though she were one of the Raksha.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Looks great! <br /> <br /> Shaping Ritual #1: This is roughly comparable to Pact With an Ifrit Lord's second SR, but Craft can generate a <b>lot</b> more sux. I'd strongly suggest capping the number.<br /> <br /> Shaping Ritual #2: Seemed fine in the book, should be fine still. I'm not personally fond of how it encourages Control Spell spam, but it shouldn't break anything.<br /> <br /> Shaping Ritual #3: I always thought the ritual you're basing this off of needed a no-stacking clause. Since this is narrower, this could stand to have a slight buff such as a +1 to the sm gained.<br /> <br /> Paint to Canvas Method: A bonus die Merit is generally \u2022\u2022\u2022, since it's a capbreaker that stacks with everything.<br /> <br /> The Painted Lotus: I don't see the purpose. Can't I already do this by Stunting the desired description? If this is intended to have mechanical effects they need to be made clearer.<br /> <br /> Master of Creativity: I feel both this and the original are massively overcosted. I'd personally price them at \u2022 or (-).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T16:35:57-08:00","id":1366653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364158-player-wants-to-make-a-character-that-can-make-paintings-come-to-life?p=1366651#post1366651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looks great! <br /> <br /> Shaping Ritual #1: This is roughly comparable to Pact With an Ifrit Lord's second SR, but Craft can generate a <b>lot</b> more sux. I'd strongly suggest capping the number.<br /> <br /> Shaping Ritual #2: Seemed fine in the book, should be fine still. I'm not personally fond of how it encourages Control Spell spam, but it shouldn't break anything.<br /> <br /> Shaping Ritual #3: I always thought the ritual you're basing this off of needed a no-stacking clause. Since this is narrower, this could stand to have a slight buff such as a +1 to the sm gained.<br /> <br /> Paint to Canvas Method: A bonus die Merit is generally \u2022\u2022\u2022, since it's a capbreaker that stacks with everything.<br /> <br /> The Painted Lotus: I don't see the purpose. Can't I already do this by Stunting the desired description? If this is intended to have mechanical effects they need to be made clearer.<br /> <br /> Master of Creativity: I feel both this and the original are massively overcosted. I'd personally price them at \u2022 or (-).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much for you feedback. I updated some of what you mentioned in the doc here! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19zoZNECHqaz31AIaRLWr_9aoRRC47DaK0xbd6mt7J2M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19zoZNECHqaz31AIaRLWr_9aoRRC47DaK0xbd6mt7J2M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19zoZNECHqaz31AIaRLWr_9aoRRC47DaK0xbd6mt7J2M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/19zoZNECHqaz31AIaRLWr_9aoRRC47DaK0xbd6mt7J2M/edit?usp=drivesdk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5059-johnsonhavoc","name":"johnsonhavoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T17:43:21-08:00","id":1366664,"title":"","content":"Just for clarification, water elementals aren't always &quot;made of water.&quot; In fact, most of the ones with write-ups appear to be made of flesh and blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}